  share of their income on energy gasoline  home heating that kind of thing one  option would be to embed a carbon tax  into a broader fiscal package such that  the regressivity of the  carbon tax could be counterbalanced by  other parts of that package that are  progressive a lot of people fear what  would happen is once you establish a  carbon tax basically they wouldn't  return it to the public they wouldn't  return it as a rebate to taxpayers or as  a reduction at one-for-one reduction in  their payroll taxes instead it would  just be another tax so you would  increase government spending you would  slow down the economy and you would have  less leave less money in the pockets of  the the working people of America and if  prices get too high people would start  to look elsewhere for cheaper products  like China I was just in China and June  when you drive through that country you  can see examples of strip-mining  clear-cutting  I mean it's blatant disregard for the  environment the United States uses the  energy to produce a g-dog GDP much more  efficiently than either China or India  does so if you're moving an activity  from the United States over to China and  India they're very likely to use a lot  more energy to produce the same product  that you could have produced with less  energy here at home  thus harming the environment overall  seeing as a fully enforced worldwide  carbon tax isn't realistic is a carbon  tax still our best option to reduce  emissions I think they're going to be a  number of unpalatable choices and the  question is could a carbon tax feature  into a set of choices that that creates  space for for an overall deal I think it  could the cost of implementing  government policy may be a lot higher  than the benefits that you're going to  try to get out of them so you have to be  very careful about that a clean simple  carbon tax rebating all the money back  to individual Americans that might work  but anything more complicating that is  very likely to cost a lot more than the  benefits that we could hope to get out  of it politics do complicate things and  betting on a clean simple carbon tax is  very risky the best way to stimulate  innovation is through market  competitiveness the more competition you  have in the free market the more  incentive there is for a businessperson  and a business  to do what it can to gain market share  and grow we are already running as  efficient as we believe being the most  price competitive producer in the world
 

